//! `g_trans_cart2jI[]`, which `g_c2s[l].cart2j_lt_*` / `.cart2j_gt_*` index).
//!
//! DO NOT hand-edit. Regenerate via `cargo run -p xtask -- gen-c2spinor-table`;
//! `--check` re-derives and fails closed if this file has drifted from the
//! vendored C source.
//!
//! # Layout
//!
//! For each `l`, block `l` is `CJ_OFFSET[l]..CJ_OFFSET[l + 1]` and holds the
//! LT block (`j = l - 1/2`, `2l` rows) followed immediately by the GT block
//! (`j = l + 1/2`, `2l + 2` rows). Every row is `2 * ncart(l)` values: the
//! `ncart(l)` alpha-spinor coefficients, then the `ncart(l)` beta ones, over
//! Cartesian components in libcint ordering. LT-then-GT adjacency is what
//! libcint's `kappa == 0` path relies on when it over-reads from the LT
//! pointer into GT, so it is preserved rather than re-derived.
//!
//! `c2spinor::tests::generated_table_matches_the_hand_transcribed_tables`
//! pins the `l <= 4` blocks against `c2spinor_coeffs.rs`, bit for bit.

